  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nNo major changes were made to the long term forecast period. High\npressure remains centered, as mentioned, over the Texas and \nLouisiana gulf coast, while the axis of the ridge extends into \nportions of the central Great Plains. PoPs for the rest of the\ncontinue to show likely (>55%) precipitation over much of the\narea, but rain chances still have room to decrease in the coming\ndays due to uncertainties regarding storm mode. This weekend into\nearly next week, the weather pattern may shift back to drier and\nwarmer conditions as high pressure moves more overhead of the\nregion. We'll have to wait for our next cold front to drop our\ntemperatures back down to being average or below average.\n\nRangel",
